WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.296
Each showcase opens in Playground.

2
00:00:02.296 --> 00:00:06.966
You can try a supplied trained model immediately, without waiting for training.

3
00:00:06.966 --> 00:00:12.026
These are three different jobs: choosing a move, answering a story question, and

4
00:00:12.026 --> 00:00:14.750
reporting what a receiver has been told.

5
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:21.381
For Ava, use Watch Ava for a journey or One move for a

6
00:00:21.381 --> 00:00:22.217
single decision.

7
00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:25.977
The model selects actions; a teacher doesn't correct them.

8
00:00:25.977 --> 00:00:31.408
This saved model reaches the lamp in fifteen moves in its practice room.

9
00:00:31.408 --> 00:00:34.750
One successful journey doesn't establish reliable navigation everywhere.

10
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.050
For Chatbot, start with an example.

11
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:42.250
This story asks who has the ball, and the model answers Cy.

12
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:46.800
Each request is independent, so include the necessary facts in the same input.

13
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.650
Use the language guide when changing a name, object or place.

14
00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.159
The colour example exposes a mistake.

15
00:00:54.159 --> 00:00:58.391
The last paint action says blue, but this model answers unknown.

16
00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:01.854
That is a real prediction, not a programmed refusal.

17
00:01:01.854 --> 00:01:06.857
Use the failure to decide what practice to add, then train and ask

18
00:01:06.857 --> 00:01:07.241
again.

19
00:01:07.241 --> 00:01:09.550
Extra practice doesn't guarantee a fix.

20
00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.740
For Device messaging, choose an asset location, leave delivery checked, and send the

21
00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:16.124
event.

22
00:01:16.124 --> 00:01:18.426
The model interprets the message history.

23
00:01:18.426 --> 00:01:21.881
With the river update delivered, its report is river.

24
00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.800
No physical hardware is connected.

25
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.559
Now choose dock and turn delivery off.

26
00:01:27.559 --> 00:01:31.214
The simulated asset moves, but the hub hasn't been told.

27
00:01:31.214 --> 00:01:33.042
The model still reports river.

28
00:01:33.042 --> 00:01:34.870
That distinction is the challenge.

29
00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:39.622
Clear the stream to start a new case; use Training if you want

30
00:01:39.622 --> 00:01:41.450
to change the model's practice.

31
00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:47.150
After training, return here and try the same input, then a variation.

32
00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:51.275
Playing doesn't teach the model, and more practice isn't automatically better.

33
00:01:51.275 --> 00:01:56.150
Look for where its predictions hold up, where they change, and where they

34
00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:56.900
still fail.
